            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous rupture of an ovarian artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e7-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajog.2008.09.875</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous rupture of an ovarian artery aneurysm is rare and is thought to be related to pregnancy or uterine fibroids. A patient without fibroids presented with extreme pain during normal menstruation. Ruptured ovarian artery aneurysm should be suspected in a multiparous woman with flank or abdominal pain and peritoneal signs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
